  identity: "cheap_question_through_an_expensive_carrier" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a cheap question is asked through an EXPENSIVE CARRIER, and the cost is charged to the question** (INVALID STATE: a claim needs one narrow fact -- does this trigger list contain merge_group -- and reaches it by naming a carrier that must be forced whole to yield it. `gunbc.merge_queue_admission` `floor_workflow_admits_merge_group` read the FIELD `witness_floor_workflow.on`, which forces the entire `Workflow` value -- every job, step, matrix and env row of the required floor emission -- to answer a membership test over a four-element list. The narrow producer already existed beside it: `gunbc.witness.witness_floor_workflow` `witness_floor_triggers()`, which the workflow own `on:` field is literally bound to, so reading the function is not a copy of the authority but IS the authority. ",
    "HARM: the cost lands on the CLAIM and not on the carrier, so the arithmetic that would locate it is never done -- the claim text looks cheap, its measured cost is not, and the difference is invisible in every artifact except a per-claim cost ledger. Five such claims were reported `budget_interrupted` by the required floor per-claim budget, which is not `claims_failed`: the PR goes red with a disposition naming no failing claim, and the author first move is to look for a defect in the claim logic, where there is none. ",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACT: the defect is a COST SHAPE and not a magnitude, so it does not scale with the question. Measured on the same five claims in `dag/test/claim/merge_queue_admission_witness_test.dag`, every column located BY NAME from `required_floor_claim_cost.tsv` (identity, module, outcome, verdict_reached, wall_ms, cpu_ms, eval_steps, cost_line_ms), before from run 33750639005 and after from 33754056276: interrupted at cpu 501 and 151552 steps becomes pass at cpu 0 and 35 steps; 501 and 155648 becomes 0 and 82; 502 and 139264 becomes 0 and 86; 507 and 143187 becomes 0 and 109; 505 and 131072 becomes 0 and 154. The `outcome` column carries the verdict without arithmetic. ",
    "A CORRECTION THAT IS PART OF THE ROW, because the first report of this class was wrong in a way this ledger should not repeat: those after-figures were first published as MILLISECONDS -- 35 to 154ms, 3.2x to 14x under the line -- because the artifact was read by column INDEX, where index 7 is `eval_steps` and `cpu_ms` is index 6. `gunbc.floor_cost_distribution` documents that `eval_steps` was INSERTED between artifact vintages precisely so an index-keyed parser reads the wrong column. A derived 93 percent carrier share was arithmetic across two units and was withdrawn entirely rather than restated. Locate by NAME. ",
    "REMEDY, and it is construction rather than a budget: read the narrowest producer that already denotes the fact, and where none exists the missing producer is the finding. Raising a deadline or exempting the claim treats the magnitude and leaves the shape, and DESIGN section 6 bare-minimum-cost rule refuses that trade independently of realised n -- n is small here is not a time-stable fact, because the next consumer of the carrier changes n. ",
    "RUNG: mitigatable. Nothing refuses a field read whose forcing cost exceeds its consumer demand, and the cost ledger is a DETECTOR that fires only after the claim is authored, enrolled and interrupted, which is why these five were found by a red and not by review. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as the capability rather than an artifact: a demanded-extent producer -- the substrate deciding, per read, which sub-graph of the carrier the consumer actually demands -- sufficient to refuse or to narrow a read that forces strictly more than its consumer observes. A cost line is NOT that trigger: a line separates expensive from cheap and says nothing about whether the expense was DEMANDED.)",
  ],

